pickups.stage.ts:11-14:
  const ui = raceStage(root, { phase: 'racing', countdown: 0, raceTick: 1460, racers, at: AT });
  // raceStage's view has no pickups; sync once more as a pickup track would.
  const { centre } = stageTrack();
  ui.sync({ phase: 'racing', countdown: 0, raceTick: 1460, racers, pickups: [true, false, true] }, AT.map((a) => carOnTrack(centre, a)));
This repeats stage.ts:113-116:
  ui.sync({ phase: o.phase, countdown: o.countdown, raceTick: o.raceTick, racers: o.racers }, o.at.map((a) => carOnTrack(track.centre, a)));
The first sync runs `legend.setPowerUp(false)` and the second runs `setPowerUp(true)`. The stage therefore renders through two syncs and an in-between state with no POWER-UP keycap, only because `raceStage` cannot pass `pickups`.

fixes.summary:
The finding is about weak tests, not a code bug. The lateral offset in `src/sim/track.ts` is already correct: (cos h, sin h)·lateral points right of the driving direction (sin h, −cos h), the same convention as propRows' 'right' side. So I changed nothing in `src/`.

I added one new test file, `tests/sim/pickup-lateral.test.ts`, that pins the offset down using only the public sim API (`validateTrack`, `trackLayout`):
- On validated copies of Dust Bowl and Bramble Bends, it adds pickups at at=0.5 with lateral +3 and −3, plus one with lateral 0. It checks:
  - the two side boxes are 6 ± 0.05 apart;
  - their midpoint is within 1.5 of the centreline;
  - the +3 box is 3 from the midpoint, on the right of the centreline direction (taken from neighbouring centre samples, dot with (−dz, dx) > 2.9) and nearly perpendicular to it;
  - the lateral-0 box sits on the centreline.
- On Dust Bowl's own data, it checks that boxes in the same row are |Δlateral| apart (3.5 / 7).

Red/green: the mutation that drops the lateral offset (`{x: p.x, z: p.z}`) fails all 3 tests. The one that flips its sign fails the 2 side-checking tests. With the real code all 3 pass. `pnpm typecheck` is clean and `pnpm test` passes: 113 files, 749 tests.
